
# PENDING — this section is deliberately empty.
#
# makeResult needs a ctx carrying a constructed Spec AND Result, built via
# the SDK's own NewSpec/NewResult constructors, plus the absent-error path
# for each. The runner builds ctx from a literal map and has no constructor
# hook, so these cannot be expressed here yet — covered per-language today
# (e.g. go's makeResult-basic / -no-spec / -no-result), which is exactly the
# drift this corpus exists to remove. Promoting it needs a runner change,
# not just fixture data.
#
# An empty `set` runs ZERO cases. Runners must not treat that as a pass by
# accident: the language runners keep a PENDING list, and corpus.test.ts
# asserts that every empty fixture is declared there AND explains itself —
# so an accidentally-blanked fixture fails the build while a knowingly
# deferred one does not.

# Machine-readable so the corpus guard can check it; the prose above
# is the long form.
basic: pending: 'Needs a ctx carrying a Spec AND Result built via the SDK constructors; the runner builds ctx from a literal map and has no constructor hook.'
basic: set: []
